 habits and physical activity levels, significantly influence obesity rates. Understanding these determinants is essential for developing effective public health strategies aimed at reducing obesity prevalence. Interventions that promote healthy lifestyle choices can help mitigate the impact of environmental factors on obesity [Data: Relationships (9032, 5896, 5901, 5904, +more)].\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n5930,BYPASS GÁSTRICO,\"BYPASS GÁSTRICO is a type of weight-loss surgery that involves altering the digestive system to assist patients in losing weight. This mixed surgical technique reduces the size of the stomach and modifies the digestive process, creating a small pouch from the stomach that is directly connected to the small intestine. While effective for weight loss, bypass gástrico can lead to complications similar to those associated with biliopancreatic diversion, particularly when performed distally or using pure restrictive techniques. Additionally, it is often linked with the dumping syndrome, a condition that can occur after the surgery. Overall, bypass gástrico is recognized as a bariatric surgery aimed at promoting significant weight loss through these surgical modifications.\",13\r\n2137,ACIDOS GRASOS ESENCIALES,\"Essential fatty acids, known as \"\"ácidos grasos esenciales,\"\" are vital nutrients necessary for the proper functioning of the human body. These include linoleic and linolenic acids, which are crucial for maintaining health and must be obtained through diet, as the body cannot synthesize them. A deficiency in essential fatty acids can lead to various health issues, including conditions such as hepatic steatosis. Therefore, ensuring an adequate intake of these fatty acids is important for overall well-being.\",4\r\n2131,LIPIDOS,\"LIPIDOS, or lipids, are a group of organic compounds that are insoluble in water, including fats and oils. They play crucial roles in biological functions and are